    "restatement": "A restatement is a full corrected filing and supersedes the prior reported state only from its own acceptance/availability time.",
    "new_holdings": "An add-new-holdings amendment supplements the public state only from its own acceptance/availability time; it must not be backdated to the report quarter.",
    "confidentiality": "Confidential-treatment denial/expiry can create add-only amendments long after quarter-end. The SEC FAQ says the amendment must be filed within six business days of denial/expiry; multiple amendments may be necessary.",
    "feature_availability": "Use SEC acceptance as the event clock and conservatively make it tradable no earlier than the next regular session after acceptance. This is not independent proof of exact first public dissemination."
